assistant: Subject: Follow next_cursor and convert cents in search_products

The `search_products` handler only read the first page from `/products` and never looked at `next_cursor`. The 2026-10-01 vendor version pages its results (5 items, `next_cursor: "5"`, `total: 7`), so the tool returned 5 of the 7 cable matches. That same version also sends prices in cents: p-1101 is 69 in the v1 fixture and 6900 in the alert, and the old code passed 6900 through as US dollars. The handler now keeps requesting pages with `&cursor=…` until `next_cursor` is empty. When the `vendor-api-version` header is 2026-10-01 or later, it divides prices by 100. I haven't seen a recorded response for the second page or a v2 price beyond the five in the alert, so the cents rule is based on that one header date. v1 responses have no cursor and an older header, so their output is unchanged; typecheck, lint and all 13 tests pass. `get_product` will probably have the same cents problem under the new version, but I left it unchanged because no recorded response proves it.

